    "['set interfaces [interface_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI configuration for the given Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. The interface naming changes from \"ge-0/0/1\" in Juniper to \"GigabitEthernet0/0/1\" in HUAWEI\\n2. The subinterface unit concept is replaced with direct .0 notation\\n3. The address format changes from CIDR (11.1.1.1/24) to traditional IP+mask (11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0)\\n4. MPLS family is enabled with a simple \"mpls\" command in HUAWEI instead of unit-level configuration', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI configuration for the given Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. The interface naming changes from \"ge-0/0/1\" in Juniper to \"GigabitEthernet0/0/1\" in HUAWEI\\n2. The subinterface unit concept is replaced with direct .0 notation\\n3. The address format changes from CIDR (11.1.1.1/24) to traditional IP+mask (11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0)\\n4. MPLS family is enabled with a simple \"mpls\" command in HUAWEI instead of unit-level configuration', 'trans_template': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI configuration for the given Juniper commands:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nThe translation:\\n1. The interface naming changes from \"ge-0/0/1\" in Juniper to \"GigabitEthernet0/0/1\" in HUAWEI\\n2. The subinterface unit concept is replaced with direct .0 notation\\n3. The address format changes from CIDR (11.1.1.1/24) to traditional IP+mask (11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0)\\n4. MPLS family is enabled with a simple \"mpls\" command in HUAWEI instead of unit-level configuration', 'trans_template': 'mpls'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type] address [ip_address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Huawei equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nThe Huawei configuration:\\n1. Uses \"interface GigabitEthernet\" instead of \"ge\" for the interface naming\\n2. Doesn\\'t require explicit unit numbering (Huawei uses main interface by default)\\n3. Uses subnet mask format (255.255.255.0) instead of prefix length (/24)\\n4. The IP address assignment is done directly under the interface context', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Huawei equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1\\n ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nThe Huawei configuration:\\n1. Uses \"interface GigabitEthernet\" instead of \"ge\" for the interface naming\\n2. Doesn\\'t require explicit unit numbering (Huawei uses main interface by default)\\n3. Uses subnet mask format (255.255.255.0) instead of prefix length (/24)\\n4. The IP address assignment is done directly under the interface context', 'trans_template': 'ip address 11.1.1.1 255.255.255.0'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.0', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration for the Juniper MPLS interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.0\\n mpls\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nIn Huawei devices:\\n1. The interface naming follows \"GigabitEthernetX/X/X\" format instead of Juniper\\'s \"ge-X/X/X\"\\n2. The \"family mpls\" configuration in Juniper is simply \"mpls\" under the interface subinterface in Huawei\\n3. The commands are applied under the specific subinterface (with dot notation like .0) just like Juniper', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration for the Juniper MPLS interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.0\\n mpls\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nIn Huawei devices:\\n1. The interface naming follows \"GigabitEthernetX/X/X\" format instead of Juniper\\'s \"ge-X/X/X\"\\n2. The \"family mpls\" configuration in Juniper is simply \"mpls\" under the interface subinterface in Huawei\\n3. The commands are applied under the specific subinterface (with dot notation like .0) just like Juniper', 'trans_template': 'mpls'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration for the Juniper MPLS interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.0\\n mpls\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nIn Huawei devices:\\n1. The interface naming follows \"GigabitEthernetX/X/X\" format instead of Juniper\\'s \"ge-X/X/X\"\\n2. The \"family mpls\" configuration in Juniper is simply \"mpls\" under the interface subinterface in Huawei\\n3. The commands are applied under the specific subinterface (with dot notation like .0) just like Juniper', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Huawei configuration for the Juniper MPLS interface configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/0.0\\n mpls\\ninterface GigabitEthernet0/0/1.0\\n mpls\\n##\\n\\nIn Huawei devices:\\n1. The interface naming follows \"GigabitEthernetX/X/X\" format instead of Juniper\\'s \"ge-X/X/X\"\\n2. The \"family mpls\" configuration in Juniper is simply \"mpls\" under the interface subinterface in Huawei\\n3. The commands are applied under the specific subinterface (with dot notation like .0) just like Juniper', 'trans_template': 'mpls'}]]": 1,
    "['set interfaces [interface_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface LoopBack0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interface LoopBack0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Huawei equivalent command for configuring the loopback interface:\\n\\n##\\ninterface LoopBack0\\n ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255\\n##\\n\\nThe Huawei configuration:\\n1. Uses \"interface LoopBack0\" instead of \"interfaces lo0 unit 0\"\\n2. Uses \"ip address\" instead of \"family inet address\"\\n3. Uses dotted decimal subnet mask (255.255.255.255) instead of prefix length (/32)\\n4. Doesn\\'t require explicit family specification as it\\'s implied by the ip address command\\n5. Huawei uses capital \"L\" in \"LoopBack\" interface naming', 'trans_template': 'interface LoopBack0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Huawei equivalent command for configuring the loopback interface:\\n\\n##\\ninterface LoopBack0\\n ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255\\n##\\n\\nThe Huawei configuration:\\n1. Uses \"interface LoopBack0\" instead of \"interfaces lo0 unit 0\"\\n2. Uses \"ip address\" instead of \"family inet address\"\\n3. Uses dotted decimal subnet mask (255.255.255.255) instead of prefix length (/32)\\n4. Doesn\\'t require explicit family specification as it\\'s implied by the ip address command\\n5. Huawei uses capital \"L\" in \"LoopBack\" interface naming', 'trans_template': 'ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [unit_number] family [family_type] address [ip_address]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface LoopBack0', 'parent_command': ['interface LoopBack0'], 'root': 'interface LoopBack0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated configuration command for HUAWEI:\\n\\n##\\ninterface LoopBack0\\n ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255\\n##\\n\\nThe command configures the loopback interface (LoopBack0) with the IPv4 address 2.2.2.9/32 in HUAWEI's CLI syntax.\", 'trans_template': 'interface LoopBack0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255', 'parent_command': ['interface LoopBack0'], 'root': 'interface LoopBack0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated configuration command for HUAWEI:\\n\\n##\\ninterface LoopBack0\\n ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255\\n##\\n\\nThe command configures the loopback interface (LoopBack0) with the IPv4 address 2.2.2.9/32 in HUAWEI's CLI syntax.\", 'trans_template': 'ip address 2.2.2.9 255.255.255.255'}]]": 1,
