    "['term [term_number] then next-hop self', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'route-policy policy1 permit node 1', 'parent_command': ['qppb local-policy [parameter1]'], 'root': 'qppb local-policy [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI command for the Juniper `set policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 1 then next-hop self` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-policy policy1 permit node 1\\napply ip next-hop 11.1.1.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: In HUAWEI devices, the \"next-hop self\" concept is implemented by explicitly specifying the local address (11.1.1.1 in this case, which matches the BGP local-address from the original configuration) rather than using a \"self\" keyword. The command structure is different as Huawei uses route-policy with nodes instead of Juniper\\'s policy-statement with terms.', 'trans_template': 'route-policy policy1 permit node 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'apply ip next-hop 11.1.1.1', 'parent_command': ['qppb local-policy [parameter1]'], 'root': 'qppb local-policy [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI command for the Juniper `set policy-options policy-statement policy1 term 1 then next-hop self` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nroute-policy policy1 permit node 1\\napply ip next-hop 11.1.1.1\\n##\\n\\nNote: In HUAWEI devices, the \"next-hop self\" concept is implemented by explicitly specifying the local address (11.1.1.1 in this case, which matches the BGP local-address from the original configuration) rather than using a \"self\" keyword. The command structure is different as Huawei uses route-policy with nodes instead of Juniper\\'s policy-statement with terms.', 'trans_template': 'apply ip next-hop 11.1.1.1'}]]": 1,
    "['term [term_number] then [action]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 11.1.1.2 as-number 100', 'parent_command': ['qppb local-policy [parameter1]'], 'root': 'qppb local-policy [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\npeer 11.1.1.2 as-number 100\\nipv4-family unicast\\n  policy policy1 export\\n  peer 11.1.1.2 enable\\n##\\nNote: The Huawei equivalent requires creating the BGP peer relationship and applying the policy in the BGP configuration context, rather than as a separate policy statement. The \"accept\" action is implied by applying the policy as an export policy to the BGP peer. The actual policy definitions (like setting next-hop self) would be configured separately under route-policy configuration in Huawei.', 'trans_template': 'peer 11.1.1.2 as-number 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv4-family unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\npeer 11.1.1.2 as-number 100\\nipv4-family unicast\\n  policy policy1 export\\n  peer 11.1.1.2 enable\\n##\\nNote: The Huawei equivalent requires creating the BGP peer relationship and applying the policy in the BGP configuration context, rather than as a separate policy statement. The \"accept\" action is implied by applying the policy as an export policy to the BGP peer. The actual policy definitions (like setting next-hop self) would be configured separately under route-policy configuration in Huawei.', 'trans_template': 'ipv4-family unicast'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'policy policy1 export', 'parent_command': ['qppb local-policy [parameter1]'], 'root': 'qppb local-policy [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\npeer 11.1.1.2 as-number 100\\nipv4-family unicast\\n  policy policy1 export\\n  peer 11.1.1.2 enable\\n##\\nNote: The Huawei equivalent requires creating the BGP peer relationship and applying the policy in the BGP configuration context, rather than as a separate policy statement. The \"accept\" action is implied by applying the policy as an export policy to the BGP peer. The actual policy definitions (like setting next-hop self) would be configured separately under route-policy configuration in Huawei.', 'trans_template': 'policy policy1 export'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 11.1.1.2 enable', 'parent_command': ['qppb local-policy [parameter1]'], 'root': 'qppb local-policy [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\npeer 11.1.1.2 as-number 100\\nipv4-family unicast\\n  policy policy1 export\\n  peer 11.1.1.2 enable\\n##\\nNote: The Huawei equivalent requires creating the BGP peer relationship and applying the policy in the BGP configuration context, rather than as a separate policy statement. The \"accept\" action is implied by applying the policy as an export policy to the BGP peer. The actual policy definitions (like setting next-hop self) would be configured separately under route-policy configuration in Huawei.', 'trans_template': 'peer 11.1.1.2 enable'}]]": 1,
